{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1344552-aeon-where-are-you-planing-on-starting-a-campaign","id":1344552,"title":"Aeon - Where are you planing on starting a Campaign?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-29T19:21:49-07:00","id":1344552,"title":"Aeon - Where are you planing on starting a Campaign?","content":"Now that the actual books have shipped and groups now have them in their hands, chances are that many are soon to explore the Era of Psions that is Aeon.<br /> <br /> So I have a simple question for any groups that plan on running campaigns in this setting... where will you be starting and what will your likely focus be?<br /> <br /> To be fair, I will share my intent. I recently managed to convince my local game group to try Aeon since we've been floating from game to game for a bit. While I am not usually the group's Storyteller, I am the one most familiar with the setting and have put together a simple (likely one-shot) adventure for them. For this game they will be playing Psions that have been hired to be part of the Aeon Trinity's rescue mission to <i>The Pandora</i>. For those unfamiliar with <i>The Pandora</i>, it is the name of the Leviathan Jump-Ship sent to make contact with the Coalition Ark after the first mission ended in disaster. While <i>The Pandora</i> didn't suffer the same kind of fate as its predecessor, they did eventually learn that the Coalition was up to something and was being deliberately deceptive for some unknown reason. When Psions on the crew discovered the presence of a large area of Quantum Corruption, they feared the presence of Aberrants... either working with or controlling the Coalition and warned the rest of <i>The Pandora's</i> crew. <i>The Pandora</i> then tried to extract the crew members still on board the Ark but was forced to abandon a sizable portion when it became clear that the Coalition had no intent of letting any of them escape. While <i>The Pandora</i> was able to escape, its Tesser Jump-Engines were crippled and they were only able to send a short message requesting rescue before they went silent.<br /> <br /> This is where my adventure will start, only 24 hours since the Aeon Trinity received the rescue request. They have already informed the United Nations of the situation... at least what they know of it and have gotten the green light to send a rescue mission. With speed of the essence (and with the Upeo wa Macho not yet returned to Earth (setting this about a month or so before their return), the Aeon Trinity has turned this matter over to Section Minerva to acquire any and all assets needed as quickly as possible. Now while Section Minerva does have access to a Leviathan Jump-Ship, it is currently only manned by a skeleton crew. Additionally, many of the ideal personnel that would be contacted for such a mission are currently unavailable due to the time constraints, thus Section Minerva has decided to entice the PCs (each a moderately experienced Psion) with whatever is needed to get them to sign on. Of course Section Minerva isn't being stupid about this, but they do need results quickly so are willing to cut some fairly generous terms with the PCs who will be told quite frankly what they are getting into and why Aeon is being so generous (desperate). Note that the PCs are being told that this is being backed specifically by the Aeon Trinity (since Section Minerva doesn't officially exist).<br /> <br /> So yes, the PCs will be the some of the only Psions on the rescue vessel (the crew will have one Psion from each of the Orders currently known to be active on Earth, with the PCs being some of them). They will not be in charge of the mission directly, but will be kept informed as Freelance Specialists. They will also be part of the group that boards the Pandora to discover the fate of that crew (do I need to say that for the most part, it isn't good?). Yes, I will be including a number of NPCs to make their missions more plausible, but they will be the main focus in this adventure, which while light on combat over all, will have some intense combat scenes in due course. Mostly I just want to introduce my group to the game overall with some intense scenes, both combat but mostly character interactions.<br /> <br /> Of course, as anyone who has looked into the Storyteller only section will know, the mission sent to rescue <i>The Pandora's</i> crew also launched a small scale raid on the Coalition Ark afterwards to liberate those that the Coalition had captured. That too will be included in this first adventure, along with a number of soldiers and Psions remaining on board to aid with the rebellion of a number of Coalition phyles to slow down the Ark and prevent the creation of Coalition Aberrants... but for the most part I intend to have the PCs be among those who leave to warn Earth about the Coalition's intentions. From here, if my group is interested in continuing this campaign, I will likely have them take part in preparing Earth for the arrival of the Ark (which at current speed is expected in just over 10 years), likely getting caught up with the Chromatic's attack on the Solar System and the rebuilding afterwards (believing they still have plenty of time before the Coalition arrives). All in all, they will likely be on the forefront of the three major battles that will help to shape the future of humanity (but with the strongest connection to the Coalition threat).<br /> <br /> So... what do other groups have planned (without spoiling too much if you feel your players are likely to find this topic)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T05:01:59-07:00","id":1344634,"title":"","content":"I did a session zero, and the general consensus was a Legions game, specifically the 2nd Legion. So, my first session was them being sent to Bosnia for a hostage situation. They were doing okay vs. the mercenaries but had to flee when a Nemesis aberrant showed up. The next two and a half sessions were basically all about what the characters wanted to do during their downtime between missions. I'll be sending them on another mission this next session, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}